description:
The VectorStatusWithDialog wrapper component currently passes db={null} and repository={null} to ManageEmbeddingSetsDialog, making the dialog completely non-functional.

## Problem
- Dialog's loadSets() returns early if !db (line 102)
- All CRUD operations require valid repository
- UI shows 'Loading sets...' indefinitely or 'No embedding sets yet' even when sets exist

## Solution
Update wrapper to access database hooks:

```typescript
export function VectorStatusWithDialog() {
  const [manageDialogOpen, setManageDialogOpen] = useState(false);
  const db = usePGliteDatabase();
  const repository = useMemo(() => 
    db ? new EmbeddingSetsRepository(db) : null, [db]);

  return (
    <>
      <VectorStatusWithDb onManageEmbeddingSets={() => setManageDialogOpen(true)} />
      {manageDialogOpen && (
        <ManageEmbeddingSetsDialog
          open={manageDialogOpen}
          onOpenChange={setManageDialogOpen}
          db={db}
          repository={repository}
          onSetSelected={() => setManageDialogOpen(false)}
        />
      )}
    </>
  );
}
```

