The ModelRegistryManager.listModels() only returns registry.models, ignoring registry.hosted. This causes hosted providers (OpenAI/Voyage/Cohere) to have undefined modelConfig.

## Problem
- listModels() returns only registry.models (line 19-20 in model-registry.ts)
- Hosted providers stored in registry.hosted are ignored
- UI falls back to default 768D for hosted models
- Embedding sets created with wrong dimensions
- Vector mismatches in subsequent operations

## Solution
Update listModels() to merge both sections:

```typescript
export function listModels(): Record<string, ModelConfig> {
  const result = { ...registry.models };

  // Add hosted providers with proper model keys
  Object.entries(registry.hosted).forEach(([provider, models]) => {
    Object.entries(models).forEach(([modelId, config]) => {
      const modelKey = `${provider}::${modelId}`;
      result[modelKey] = config;
    });
  });

  return result;
}
```

## Files
- packages/embeddings/src/model-registry.ts

## Impact
Critical for embedding set creation to use correct dimensions for hosted models.

